<div class="wp-block-group grid is-layout-grid wp-container-core-group-is-layout-1bc9c2ce wp-block-group-is-layout-grid">
<div class="wp-block-group content is-content-justification-left is-layout-constrained wp-container-core-group-is-layout-dcb074c1 wp-block-group-is-layout-constrained"><h2 class="has-link-color wp-elements-5 wp-block-post-title has-text-color has-warm-brown-color">Cookies and Cream Cookies</h2>


<div class="wp-block-group has-cocoa-color has-text-color has-link-color wp-elements-6 is-layout-flex wp-container-core-group-is-layout-76a83a37 wp-block-group-is-layout-flex" style="margin-bottom:24px"><div class="wp-block-post-date"><time datetime="2021-11-29T22:17:00-05:00">November 29, 2021</time></div>

<div class="wp-block-post-date__modified-date wp-block-post-date"><time datetime="2026-01-29T14:31:33-05:00">January 29, 2026</time></div></div>


<div class="entry-content wp-elements-7 wp-block-post-content has-text-color has-cocoa-color is-layout-flow wp-container-core-post-content-is-layout-770cb1c9 wp-block-post-content-is-layout-flow">
<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><em>These are the ULTIMATE cookies and cream cookies with Oreo cookie crumbs in the cookie dough and packed full of chopped Oreos and Hershey’s cookies and cream chocolates.&nbsp;</em></p>



<figure class="wp-block-gallery has-nested-images columns-default is-cropped wp-block-gallery-4 is-layout-flex wp-block-gallery-is-layout-flex">
<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img data-perfmatters-preload decoding="async" width="682" height="1024" data-id="9865" src="https://baranbakery.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/11/cookies-and-cream-cookies-4-682x1024.jpg" alt="cookies and cream cookies" class="wp-image-9865" srcset="https://baranbakery.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/11/cookies-and-cream-cookies-4-682x1024.jpg 682w, https://baranbakery.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/11/cookies-and-cream-cookies-4-200x300.jpg 200w, https://baranbakery.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/11/cookies-and-cream-cookies-4-768x1152.jpg 768w, https://baranbakery.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/11/cookies-and-cream-cookies-4-1024x1536.jpg 1024w, https://baranbakery.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/11/cookies-and-cream-cookies-4-150x225.jpg 150w, https://baranbakery.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/11/cookies-and-cream-cookies-4-735x1103.jpg 735w, https://baranbakery.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/11/cookies-and-cream-cookies-4.jpg 1333w" sizes="(max-width: 682px) 100vw, 682px" fetchpriority="high"></figure>
</figure>



<h2 class="wp-block-heading" id="h-what-makes-these-the-best-cookies-and-cream-cookies">What makes these the best cookies and cream cookies?!</h2>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">I’m glad you asked because this recipe is most certainly adapted from my super quick &amp; easy <a href="https://baranbakery.com/small-batch-chocolate-chip-cookies/">small-batch</a> <a href="https://baranbakery.com/small-batch-chocolate-chip-cookies/">chocolate chip cookies</a> which means only one thing. They are super simple, have minimal ingredients, and are done in less than 20 minutes. Ok, that was more than one thing but YOU ARE WELCOME.&nbsp;</p>



<h2 class="wp-block-heading" id="h-how-to-make-cookies-and-cream-cookies">How to make cookies and cream cookies</h2>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">To stay on the easy and quick brand, I made sure we were using melted butter for the dough again because no one wants to wait for the butter to be at the perfect room temperature. The melted butter gets whisked with the light brown sugar, then whisk in the egg and vanilla and then fold in the flour, Oreo crumbs and baking powder, followed by the chopped Oreos and cookies and cream chocolate. Scoop, roll and bake. DONE.</p>



<figure class="wp-block-gallery has-nested-images columns-default is-cropped wp-block-gallery-5 is-layout-flex wp-block-gallery-is-layout-flex">
<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img decoding="async" width="682" height="1024" data-id="9867" src="data:image/svg+xml,%3Csvg%20xmlns='http://www.w3.org/2000/svg'%20width='682'%20height='1024'%20viewBox='0%200%20682%201024'%3E%3C/svg%3E" alt="cookies with splashing milk" class="wp-image-9867 perfmatters-lazy" data-src="https://baranbakery.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/11/oreo-cookies-3-682x1024.jpg" data-srcset="https://baranbakery.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/11/oreo-cookies-3-682x1024.jpg 682w, https://baranbakery.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/11/oreo-cookies-3-200x300.jpg 200w, https://baranbakery.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/11/oreo-cookies-3-768x1152.jpg 768w, https://baranbakery.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/11/oreo-cookies-3-1024x1536.jpg 1024w, https://baranbakery.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/11/oreo-cookies-3-150x225.jpg 150w, https://baranbakery.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/11/oreo-cookies-3-1200x1800.jpg 1200w, https://baranbakery.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/11/oreo-cookies-3.jpg 1333w" data-sizes="(max-width: 682px) 100vw, 682px" /></figure>
</figure>



<h3 class="wp-block-heading" id="h-ingredients">Ingredients:</h3>



<ul class="wp-block-list">
<li><strong>Flour</strong>: I just used all-purpose flour for this recipe however, I HIGHLY recommend using a <a href="https://www.amazon.com/gp/product/B0811RX62R/ref=as_li_tl?ie=UTF8&amp;tag=baranbakery1-20&amp;camp=1789&amp;creative=9325&amp;linkCode=as2&amp;creativeASIN=B0811RX62R&amp;linkId=cfc0295acfdaa576e17f0e2e2df87467" rel="nofollow sponsored">digital scale</a>, as over-measuring the flour is the most common baking mistake and may result in dry cookies. </li>
</ul>



<ul class="wp-block-list">
<li><strong>Sugar</strong>: I’m going to spare you my whole rant on sugar lol… I used JUST light brown sugar for these cookies and I don’t recommend substituting it. Granulated sugar makes these cookies super pale and chewy. </li>



<li><strong>Butter</strong>: I LOVE using salted butter in cookies! I started doing this this year and it just seems more flavorful and it’s one less step since you don’t have to add extra salt. If you use unsalted butter, just add ¼ tsp salt to the batter with the flour too.</li>



<li><strong>Egg</strong>: I used one FULL large egg in this recipe because no one wants to mess with separating eggs. </li>



<li><strong>Vanilla</strong>: Don’t underestimate the power of vanilla extract in a cookie recipe. I stopped putting vanilla in EVERYTHING that I make but for cookies it’s essential. </li>



<li><strong>Baking Powder</strong>: just baking powder, no baking soda. </li>



<li><strong>Chocolate</strong>: a cookie with Hershey’s cookies and cream chocolate in it has got to be the best cookie on earth… </li>



<li><strong>Oreos</strong>: 10/10 recommend adding Oreo crumbs to your cookie dough, then add more chunks in place of the chocolate chips. </li>
</ul>



<h3 class="wp-block-heading" id="h-what-kind-of-chocolate-can-i-use-for-these-cookies">What kind of chocolate can I use for these cookies?</h3>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">As I mentioned before, I use Hershey’s cookies and cream chocolate because I secretly always wanted to use it in a recipe. However, if you’re in a pinch, I usually make these with plain white chocolate chips because that&#8217;s what I have on hand. Please don’t judge me but I prefer Nestle white chocolate chips, always. What can I say?! I like cheap chocolate, lol.&nbsp;</p>



<figure class="wp-block-gallery has-nested-images columns-default is-cropped wp-block-gallery-6 is-layout-flex wp-block-gallery-is-layout-flex">
<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img decoding="async" width="682" height="1024" data-id="9866" src="data:image/svg+xml,%3Csvg%20xmlns='http://www.w3.org/2000/svg'%20width='682'%20height='1024'%20viewBox='0%200%20682%201024'%3E%3C/svg%3E" alt="baked cookies and cream cookies" class="wp-image-9866 perfmatters-lazy" data-src="https://baranbakery.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/11/cookies-and-cream-cookies-682x1024.jpg" data-srcset="https://baranbakery.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/11/cookies-and-cream-cookies-682x1024.jpg 682w, https://baranbakery.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/11/cookies-and-cream-cookies-200x300.jpg 200w, https://baranbakery.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/11/cookies-and-cream-cookies-768x1152.jpg 768w, https://baranbakery.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/11/cookies-and-cream-cookies-1024x1536.jpg 1024w, https://baranbakery.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/11/cookies-and-cream-cookies-150x225.jpg 150w, https://baranbakery.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/11/cookies-and-cream-cookies-1200x1800.jpg 1200w, https://baranbakery.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/11/cookies-and-cream-cookies.jpg 1333w" data-sizes="(max-width: 682px) 100vw, 682px" /></figure>
</figure>



<h2 class="wp-block-heading" id="h-how-to-bake-cookies-and-cream-cookies">How to bake cookies and cream cookies</h2>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">First, I recommend scooping and rolling these cookies, as opposed to just scooping them and placing blobs on a cookie sheet. This is because they have slightly less fat (butter) in the recipe than some other cookie recipes so they tend to bake in the shape they were placed. </p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Second, I always bake in a convection oven but when I took some polls on instagram, most of you said you either don’t have one or you don’t know how to use your convection oven. So since I developed ALL my recipes in a 350F convection oven, I decided to experiment with a conventional.&nbsp;</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">If you don’t know the difference, a convection oven has a fan that circulates the heat more evenly. This usually results in a quicker bake, so always do less time if you’re unsure and it also gives a more even browning. If you’re not used to it, the change can be frustrating.&nbsp;</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">If you’re using a conventional (NO FAN) oven, I recommend baking these cookies at 325F (163C) for about 12 minutes (for the 2 oz cookies) instead of 350F (177C) for 10 minutes in a convection oven.&nbsp;</p>



<figure class="wp-block-gallery has-nested-images columns-default is-cropped wp-block-gallery-7 is-layout-flex wp-block-gallery-is-layout-flex">
<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img decoding="async" width="682" height="1024" data-id="9868" src="data:image/svg+xml,%3Csvg%20xmlns='http://www.w3.org/2000/svg'%20width='682'%20height='1024'%20viewBox='0%200%20682%201024'%3E%3C/svg%3E" alt="whisk together wet ingredients and fold in dry ingredients" class="wp-image-9868 perfmatters-lazy" data-src="https://baranbakery.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/11/oreo-cookies-8-682x1024.jpg" data-srcset="https://baranbakery.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/11/oreo-cookies-8-682x1024.jpg 682w, https://baranbakery.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/11/oreo-cookies-8-200x300.jpg 200w, https://baranbakery.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/11/oreo-cookies-8-768x1152.jpg 768w, https://baranbakery.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/11/oreo-cookies-8-1024x1536.jpg 1024w, https://baranbakery.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/11/oreo-cookies-8-150x225.jpg 150w, https://baranbakery.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/11/oreo-cookies-8-1200x1800.jpg 1200w, https://baranbakery.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/11/oreo-cookies-8.jpg 1333w" data-sizes="(max-width: 682px) 100vw, 682px" /><figcaption class="wp-element-caption">whisk together wet ingredients and fold in dry ingredients</figcaption></figure>



<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img decoding="async" width="682" height="1024" data-id="9869" src="data:image/svg+xml,%3Csvg%20xmlns='http://www.w3.org/2000/svg'%20width='682'%20height='1024'%20viewBox='0%200%20682%201024'%3E%3C/svg%3E" alt="fold in Oreos chunks and white chocolate" class="wp-image-9869 perfmatters-lazy" data-src="https://baranbakery.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/11/oreo-cookies-9-682x1024.jpg" data-srcset="https://baranbakery.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/11/oreo-cookies-9-682x1024.jpg 682w, https://baranbakery.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/11/oreo-cookies-9-200x300.jpg 200w, https://baranbakery.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/11/oreo-cookies-9-768x1152.jpg 768w, https://baranbakery.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/11/oreo-cookies-9-1024x1536.jpg 1024w, https://baranbakery.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/11/oreo-cookies-9-150x225.jpg 150w, https://baranbakery.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/11/oreo-cookies-9-1200x1800.jpg 1200w, https://baranbakery.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/11/oreo-cookies-9.jpg 1333w" data-sizes="(max-width: 682px) 100vw, 682px" /><figcaption class="wp-element-caption">fold in Oreos chunks and white chocolate</figcaption></figure>
</figure>



<h2 class="wp-block-heading" id="h-frequently-asked-questions-nbsp">Frequently Asked Questions&nbsp;</h2>



<h3 class="wp-block-heading" id="h-how-can-i-store-unbaked-cookies-and-cream-cookie-dough">How can I store unbaked cookies and cream cookie dough?</h3>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">The cookie dough is pretty soft so you’ll want to scoop it out, roll it and then press it down just a little so it looks more like a disc than a ball. Then refrigerate it on a plate or tray until the cookie dough is more firm. Once they’re firm, place them in a ziplock bag and freeze. To bake, remove from the freezer as the oven is preheating and just add an additional 2-3 minutes to the bake time.</p>



<h3 class="wp-block-heading" id="h-can-i-make-these-vegan">Can I make these vegan?</h3>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Unfortunately I haven’t had time to test this but I really wanted to get this recipe out to you all so when I do try it, I’ll certainly update it. If you try it, let me know!</p>



<figure class="wp-block-gallery has-nested-images columns-default is-cropped wp-block-gallery-8 is-layout-flex wp-block-gallery-is-layout-flex">
<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img decoding="async" width="682" height="1024" data-id="9870" src="data:image/svg+xml,%3Csvg%20xmlns='http://www.w3.org/2000/svg'%20width='682'%20height='1024'%20viewBox='0%200%20682%201024'%3E%3C/svg%3E" alt="roll cookie dough into ball if baking right away" class="wp-image-9870 perfmatters-lazy" data-src="https://baranbakery.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/11/oreo-cookies-10-682x1024.jpg" data-srcset="https://baranbakery.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/11/oreo-cookies-10-682x1024.jpg 682w, https://baranbakery.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/11/oreo-cookies-10-200x300.jpg 200w, https://baranbakery.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/11/oreo-cookies-10-768x1152.jpg 768w, https://baranbakery.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/11/oreo-cookies-10-1024x1536.jpg 1024w, https://baranbakery.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/11/oreo-cookies-10-150x225.jpg 150w, https://baranbakery.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/11/oreo-cookies-10-1200x1800.jpg 1200w, https://baranbakery.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/11/oreo-cookies-10.jpg 1333w" data-sizes="(max-width: 682px) 100vw, 682px" /><figcaption class="wp-element-caption">roll cookie dough into ball if baking right away</figcaption></figure>



<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img decoding="async" width="682" height="1024" data-id="9871" src="data:image/svg+xml,%3Csvg%20xmlns='http://www.w3.org/2000/svg'%20width='682'%20height='1024'%20viewBox='0%200%20682%201024'%3E%3C/svg%3E" alt="roll cookie dough into discs if freezing" class="wp-image-9871 perfmatters-lazy" data-src="https://baranbakery.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/11/oreo-cookies-11-682x1024.jpg" data-srcset="https://baranbakery.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/11/oreo-cookies-11-682x1024.jpg 682w, https://baranbakery.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/11/oreo-cookies-11-200x300.jpg 200w, https://baranbakery.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/11/oreo-cookies-11-768x1152.jpg 768w, https://baranbakery.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/11/oreo-cookies-11-1024x1536.jpg 1024w, https://baranbakery.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/11/oreo-cookies-11-150x225.jpg 150w, https://baranbakery.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/11/oreo-cookies-11-1200x1800.jpg 1200w, https://baranbakery.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/11/oreo-cookies-11.jpg 1333w" data-sizes="(max-width: 682px) 100vw, 682px" /><figcaption class="wp-element-caption">roll cookie dough into discs if freezing</figcaption></figure>
</figure>



<h3 class="wp-block-heading" id="h-can-i-double-the-recipe-to-make-a-big-batch-of-cookies">Can I double the recipe to make a big batch of cookies?</h3>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">You can! I double this recipe all the time and it makes 16 normal size cookies (2 oz) or 8 large (4 oz) cookies.&nbsp;</p>



<h3 class="wp-block-heading" id="h-can-i-use-different-add-ins-nbsp">Can I use different add-ins?&nbsp;</h3>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">You sure can! As I mentioned before, you can use white chocolate chips instead of Hershey&#8217;s cookies and cream chocolate. I also think macadamia nuts or dark chocolate would be PHENOMENAL in these if you want to balance the sweetness a bit more.&nbsp;</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">If you have any other add-ins you’ve tried, let me know in the comment section.&nbsp;</p>



<figure class="wp-block-gallery has-nested-images columns-default is-cropped wp-block-gallery-9 is-layout-flex wp-block-gallery-is-layout-flex">
<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img decoding="async" width="682" height="1024" data-id="9864" src="data:image/svg+xml,%3Csvg%20xmlns='http://www.w3.org/2000/svg'%20width='682'%20height='1024'%20viewBox='0%200%20682%201024'%3E%3C/svg%3E" alt="cookies and cream cookies with bite taken out" class="wp-image-9864 perfmatters-lazy" data-src="https://baranbakery.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/11/cookies-and-cream-cookies-3-682x1024.jpg" data-srcset="https://baranbakery.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/11/cookies-and-cream-cookies-3-682x1024.jpg 682w, https://baranbakery.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/11/cookies-and-cream-cookies-3-200x300.jpg 200w, https://baranbakery.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/11/cookies-and-cream-cookies-3-768x1152.jpg 768w, https://baranbakery.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/11/cookies-and-cream-cookies-3-1024x1536.jpg 1024w, https://baranbakery.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/11/cookies-and-cream-cookies-3-150x225.jpg 150w, https://baranbakery.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/11/cookies-and-cream-cookies-3-1200x1800.jpg 1200w, https://baranbakery.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/11/cookies-and-cream-cookies-3.jpg 1333w" data-sizes="(max-width: 682px) 100vw, 682px" /></figure>
</figure>



<h2 class="wp-block-heading" id="h-how-to-store-the-cookies-after-baking">How to store the cookies after baking</h2>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">These cookies and cream cookies are also best stored in your belly… lol. Ok, jokes aside, just place them in a ziplock bag and keep them at room temperature for up to five days. They obviously will dry out a little more by day 5 but I just pop in the microwave for like 5-10 seconds before eating.&nbsp;</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Thanks so much for reading today’s post , if you have any questions just comment down below, i’m happy to answer! If you make these cookies, I would love to see them! Make sure to tag me <a href="https://www.instagram.com/baranbakery/?hl=en"><em>@baranbakery</em></a> on instagram and as always, have a blessed day and happy baking!</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><em>Love, B</em></p>


